#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:27
msgid ""
"Pass in (x, y) or (longitude, latitude) values by providing a file name to "
"an ASCII data table, a 2-D :class:`numpy.ndarray`, a :class:`pandas."
"DataFrame`, an :class:`xarray.Dataset` made up of 1-D :class:`xarray."
"DataArray` data variables, or a :class:`geopandas.GeoDataFrame` containing "
"the tabular data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:33
msgid "Arrays of x and y coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:36
msgid ""
"Name of the output netCDF grid file. If not specified, will return an :class:"
"`xarray.DataArray` object. For writing a specific grid file format or "
"applying basic data operations to the output grid, see :gmt-docs:`gmt."
"html#grd-inout-full` for the available modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:40
msgid ""
"*x_inc*\\ [**+e**\\|\\ **n**][/\\ *y_inc*\\ [**+e**\\|\\ **n**]]. *x_inc* "
"[and optionally *y_inc*] is the grid spacing.  - **Geographical (degrees) "
"coordinates**: Optionally, append an   increment unit. Choose among **m** to "
"indicate arc-minutes or   **s** to indicate arc-seconds. If one of the units "
"**e**, **f**,   **k**, **M**, **n** or **u** is appended instead, the "
"increment   is assumed to be given in meter, foot, km, mile, nautical mile "
"or   US survey foot, respectively, and will be converted to the   equivalent "
"degrees longitude at the middle latitude of the region   (the conversion "
"depends on :gmt-term:`PROJ_ELLIPSOID`). If   *y_inc* is given but set to 0 "
"it will be reset equal to *x_inc*;   otherwise it will be converted to "
"degrees latitude.  - **All coordinates**: If **+e** is appended then the "
"corresponding   max *x* (*east*) or *y* (*north*) may be slightly adjusted "
"to fit   exactly the given increment [by default the increment may be   "
"adjusted slightly to fit the given domain]. Finally, instead of   giving an "
"increment you may specify the *number of nodes* desired   by appending "
"**+n** to the supplied integer argument; the   increment is then "
"recalculated from the number of nodes, the   ``registration``, and the "
"domain. The resulting increment value   depends on whether you have selected "
"a gridline-registered or   pixel-registered grid; see :gmt-docs:`GMT File "
"Formats   <reference/file-formats.html#gmt-file-formats>` for details.  "
"**Note**: If ``region=grdfile`` is used then the grid spacing and the "
"registration have already been initialized; use ``spacing`` and "
"``registration`` to override these values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:40
msgid ""
"*x_inc*\\ [**+e**\\|\\ **n**][/\\ *y_inc*\\ [**+e**\\|\\ **n**]]. *x_inc* "
"[and optionally *y_inc*] is the grid spacing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:43
msgid ""
"**Geographical (degrees) coordinates**: Optionally, append an increment "
"unit. Choose among **m** to indicate arc-minutes or **s** to indicate arc-"
"seconds. If one of the units **e**, **f**, **k**, **M**, **n** or **u** is "
"appended instead, the increment is assumed to be given in meter, foot, km, "
"mile, nautical mile or US survey foot, respectively, and will be converted "
"to the equivalent degrees longitude at the middle latitude of the region "
"(the conversion depends on :gmt-term:`PROJ_ELLIPSOID`). If *y_inc* is given "
"but set to 0 it will be reset equal to *x_inc*; otherwise it will be "
"converted to degrees latitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:54
msgid ""
"**All coordinates**: If **+e** is appended then the corresponding max *x* "
"(*east*) or *y* (*north*) may be slightly adjusted to fit exactly the given "
"increment [by default the increment may be adjusted slightly to fit the "
"given domain]. Finally, instead of giving an increment you may specify the "
"*number of nodes* desired by appending **+n** to the supplied integer "
"argument; the increment is then recalculated from the number of nodes, the "
"``registration``, and the domain. The resulting increment value depends on "
"whether you have selected a gridline-registered or pixel-registered grid; "
"see :gmt-docs:`GMT File Formats <reference/file-formats.html#gmt-file-"
"formats>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:66
msgid ""
"**Note**: If ``region=grdfile`` is used then the grid spacing and the "
"registration have already been initialized; use ``spacing`` and "
"``registration`` to override these values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:70
msgid ""
"For large data sets you can save some memory (at the expense of more "
"processing) by only storing one form of location coordinates (geographic or "
"Cartesian 3-D vectors) at any given time, translating from one form to the "
"other when necessary [Default keeps both arrays in memory]. Not applicable "
"with ``voronoi``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:76
msgid ""
"Used to skip duplicate points since the algorithm cannot handle them. "
"[Default assumes there are no duplicates]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:79
msgid ""
"**d**\\|\\ **n**\\|\\ **z**\\ [*dist*]. Specify the quantity that should be "
"assigned to the grid nodes [Default is **d**]:  - **d**: compute distances "
"to the nearest data point - **n**: assign the ID numbers of the Voronoi "
"polygons that each   grid node is inside - **z**: assign all nodes inside "
"the polygon the z-value of the center   node for a natural nearest-neighbor "
"grid.  Optionally, append the resampling interval along Voronoi arcs in "
"spherical degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:79
msgid ""
"**d**\\|\\ **n**\\|\\ **z**\\ [*dist*]. Specify the quantity that should be "
"assigned to the grid nodes [Default is **d**]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:83
msgid "**d**: compute distances to the nearest data point"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:84
msgid ""
"**n**: assign the ID numbers of the Voronoi polygons that each grid node is "
"inside"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:86
msgid ""
"**z**: assign all nodes inside the polygon the z-value of the center node "
"for a natural nearest-neighbor grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:89
msgid ""
"Optionally, append the resampling interval along Voronoi arcs in spherical "
"degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:92
msgid ""
"Specify the unit used for distance calculations. Choose among **d** "
"(spherical degrees), **e** (meters), **f** (feet), **k** (kilometers), **M** "
"(miles), **n** (nautical miles), or **u** (survey feet)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:96
msgid ""
"Read the information pertaining to each Voronoi polygon (the unique node "
"lon, lat and polygon area) from a separate file [Default acquires this "
"information from the ASCII segment headers of the output file]. Required if "
"binary input via `voronoi` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:102
msgid ""
"Append the name of a file with pre-calculated Voronoi polygons [Default "
"performs the Voronoi construction on input data]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/sphdistance.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.sphdistance.sphdistance:105
msgid ""
"*xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax*\\ [**+r**][**+u**\\ *unit*]. Specify the :doc:`region "
"</tutorials/basics/regions>` of interest."
msgstr ""

